1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[Killua] The King's self-harm,
the existence of a third party…

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
We're still nowhere close to figuring out
what really happened.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,000
[Morel] It's time.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
One minute left to go.

5
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

6
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
[singer singing in English]

7
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

8
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
[singer singing in English]

9
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
CHARGE X AND X INVADE

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[lock clicking]

12
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
[ticking]

13
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[imperceptible]

14
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
[narrator] Two minutes
before Morel's call to arms…

15
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
two men leapt from a giant creature

16
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,000
and began their long descent
to the Republic of East Gorteau,

17
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
which expanded below.

18
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[narrator] Pitou was the first
to notice it.

19
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
"just because."

20
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Pitou's hunch was vague.

21
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
[Neferpitou] Something's coming.

22
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:17,000
[narrator] But seconds later,
faint suspicions became certainty.

23
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
[Neferpitou] The enemy.

24
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:33,000
that even Pitou's extraordinary senses
were unable to detect them at all.

25
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Now battle ready, this certainty
was a result of feral instincts

26
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
left over from Pitou's animal origin.

27
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[gasps]

28
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Pitou's En…

29
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
disappeared?

30
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
[Morel] Ten more seconds to go.

31
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Nine…

32
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Eight…

33
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Seven…

34
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
[narrator] As Morel counted down
to the impending attack,

35
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
[Morel] Six…

36
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Five…

37
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Three…

38
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Two…

39
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[gasps]

40
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
[Morel] One!

41
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Go!

42
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
[Neferpitou] Where'd they go?

43
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
in the face of a menace to the King

44
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,000
A far greater threat
than this countless rain of dragons

45
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
[narrator] When Pitou uses
this Nen ability

46
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
in order to fight at full strength,

47
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:59,000
it takes less than a tenth of a second
from activation to attack.

48
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
BAD MOVE

49
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,000
No, it's true.

50
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Think about it.

51
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:40,000
When people are near death,
time seems to slow down,

52
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
It's a similar principle.

53
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,000
In fact, I consider this phenomenon
even more credible,

54
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
You can even obtain personal information

55
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
that could only be known
by the other person,

56
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
SPIRIT ECHOES

57
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:20,000
This temporal discrepancy often occurs
when truly powerful warriors clash.

58
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
The secret behind that old fart's power?

59
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
There are several possibilities.

60
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Fool! We aren't equals.

61
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
He's always gotten the best of me.

62
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
What?

63
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
you had better look out for…

64
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:49,000
[narrator] Netero's sequential movements
appeared to be deliberate, fluid.

65
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,000
At least, that's how it looked
from Pitou's perspective.

66
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:03,000
between the activation
of Pitou's Nen ability

67
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
and the subsequent attack.

68
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Pitou was able to capture
Netero's movements by sight,

69
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
[wind blowing]

70
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:11,000
[narrator] Netero, 46 years old, winter.

71
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Sensing that he had reached
the upper limits

72
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
of his physical and martial arts skills,

73
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
he pondered and reflected,

74
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:26,000
and he realized that he was grateful.

75
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,000
for making him into the man he had become,

76
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:22,000
and he wanted to show his gratitude
in his own unique way.

77
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,000
At first, this sequence took
five to six seconds to complete.

78
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:08,000
On the first day, the 10,000 punches
took him more than 18 hours.

79
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Once finished,
he'd fall asleep on the spot.

80
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
He would wake the next day
and repeat the process.

81
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
[birds chirping]

82
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,000
[bird screeching]

83
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,000
After two years, he noticed a change.

84
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[breathing heavily]

85
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[narrator] Even after the 10,000 punches,
the sun had not yet set.

86
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[narrator] This gave him
more time to pray.

87
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
[floor creaking]

88
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
[students murmuring]

89
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:55,000
[man 1] Who the hell is this guy?
Why is he dressed that way?

90
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[man 2] I'd like to see him try, Master.

91
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
[murmurs continue]

92
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
[narrator] When Netero came down
from the mountains,

93
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:20,000
it seemed that his fists
had left sound behind them in their wake.

94
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,000
[crack echoing]

95
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
[man 4] It's like he disappeared.

96
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
[assistant] The sound came so much later.

97
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Uh, sir?

98
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
The… [weeping]

99
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Bodhisattva Guanyin.

100
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Will you defend your dojo?

101
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[instructor] This dojo is yours.

102
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:07,000
But please, please make me your pupil.

103
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
[narrator] It was the birth of a monster.

104
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Yeah, sure.
If you treat me to a real nice meal.

105
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
[static crackling]

106
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[narrator] This turn of events
took place over six decades ago.

107
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[Neferpitou] Considering
where his hands stopped,

108
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,000
that attack came from
an impossible direction. How?

109
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
I would appreciate it if you would
disappear far into the distance.

110
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,000
[Neferpitou] Damn.
I'm nowhere near where I started.

111
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[Shaiapouf] Sire!

112
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
[gasps] Pouf!

113
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,000
He can't hear me.
He's too worried about the King.

114
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Dr. Blythe!

115
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
[narrator] Normally, that's an ability

116
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:43,000
that's useless for anything
but medical treatment.

117
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:48,000
You see, Dr. Blythe cannot move
from where it's activated,

118
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:09,000
[narrator] That restriction was
just enough to keep Pitou in the fight.

119
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Faster!

120
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
[gasps]

121
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
MIDNIGHT

122
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[yawns]

123
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Hmm?

124
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
[grunts]

125
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:03,000
[narrator] There, where they had hoped
they would encounter no one at all,

126
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:11,000
[closing theme music playing]

127
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[upbeat music playing]

128
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, Monster and Monster.

129
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
